      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Add the onion and carrot and cook for 8 minutes until softened. Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the grated beetroot and cook, stirring, for 5 minutes. Pour in the tinned tomatoes and cook for 3 more minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour in the stock and add the bay leaves. Bring to a boil, then add the diced potato. Simmer for 10 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the shredded cabbage. Simmer for a further 15 to 20 minutes until all the vegetables are tender."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the bay leaves. Stir in the red wine vinegar. Taste and adjust. Ladle into bowls, top with chopped dill and a spoonful of sour cream."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Soup has lost its colour and looks brown"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the vinegar earlier in the process. Acid locks the colour of beetroot. You can also add a small amount of grated raw beetroot right at the end to revive the colour."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Soup tastes too earthy"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add a little more vinegar and a pinch of sugar to balance. Dill also lifts the earthiness significantly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Potato is falling apart"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "You added the potato too early or the dice was too small. Add it after the beetroot has had its initial cook, and aim for 2cm cubes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Borscht is the national soup of Ukraine and has been eaten there for hundreds of years. It also appears across Russia, Poland, and other Eastern European countries, each with their own version. The Ukrainian version is typically richer and more complex, with more vegetables and a full-flavoured broth. It was added to UNESCO's cultural heritage list in 2022."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
